then dress up once.","moments":[{"icon":"🌿","time":"Morning","label":"Pamplemousses botanical garden and the giant water-lily pond"},{"icon":"🎨","time":"Afternoon","label":"A painting or craft session (ask your stay; availability not checked)"},{"icon":"🕯️","time":"Evening","label":"Dinner at the resort’s best restaurant"}],"dinner":"Reserved table by the sea. Flag veg needs in advance.","image":"garden"},{"day":"Day 6","date":"Thu · 25 Feb","place":"Mauritius → Kolkata","emoji":"🏠","title":"A slow last morning.","note":"There is no direct flight to Kolkata, so the way home goes via Delhi or Mumbai. Check connection times before booking.","moments":[{"icon":"🥐","time":"Morning","label":"Slow breakfast, last souvenirs (vanilla, tea, rum)"},{"icon":"🚗","time":"Midday","label":"Transfer to the airport (timing depends on the flights)"},{"icon":"✈️","time":"Flight","label":"Mauritius → Delhi or Mumbai → Kolkata, one stop"}],"dinner":"Dinner at home.","image":"lemorne"}]},{"id":"luxury","name":"5-star beach resort","tag":"Stretch","routeLine":"Delhi → Mauritius → one-stop flight home → Kolkata","badges":["🏝️ 5 nights 5-star resort","💆 Spa and private dinner"],"budget":{"flights":140000,"stays":230000,"food":30000,"activities":35000,"local":25000},"summary":"A proper 5-star resort with spa, private beach dinner and a quiet lagoon. The most indulgent version, but February rates and the long flights push it over the ₹4L cap.","pros":["The most indulgent: spa, private dinner, quiet lagoon","Everything on one island","The classic honeymoon feel"],"cons":["About ₹4.6L all-in, so about ₹60k over the cap","February is hot, humid and rainy, with cyclone season","No direct flight to Kolkata","All prices are estimates"],"travel":[{"label":"Out · Sat 20 Feb","value":"Delhi → Mauritius, about 8 hours nonstop. Round trips run about ₹58-62k per person, an estimate from search results."},{"label":"Back · Thu 25 Feb","value":"Mauritius → Delhi or Mumbai → Kolkata, one stop."},{"label":"Flights total","value":"About ₹1.4L for two, including the hop to Kolkata. Not a live quote."},{"label":"Resort","value":"A 5-star room is about ₹40-60k a night in February (an estimate)."}],"lockFirst":{"flights":"Get live quotes first and book as one ticket each way.","stay":"A 5-star resort with spa. Ask for an exact 20-25 Feb quote and what is included.","dinner":"Book the private beach dinner for Wed 24 Feb."},"days":[{"day":"Day 1","date":"Sat · 20 Feb","place":"Delhi → Mauritius","emoji":"✈️","title":"Fly out, land by the sea.","note":"Flight and transfer take most of the day. A welcome drink and the lagoon by evening.","moments":[{"icon":"✈️","time":"Flight","label":"Delhi → Mauritius, about 8 hours nonstop (check the schedule)"},{"icon":"🚗","time":"Arrive","label":"Transfer to your resort (about 45 minutes to 1.5 hours, depending on the coast)"},{"icon":"🌅","time":"Evening","label":"Check in, sunset by the sea"}],"dinner":"A simple dinner where you are staying. Early night.","image":"sunset"},{"day":"Day 2","date":"Sun · 21 Feb","place":"North coast","emoji":"🏖️","title":"Do nothing by the lagoon.","note":"A slow first full day. Port Louis is quiet on Sundays, so keep this one for the beach.","moments":[{"icon":"🏖️","time":"Morning","label":"Beach and pool at Trou aux Biches or Grand Baie"},{"icon":"🎨","time":"Afternoon","label":"Sketch the lagoon colours"},{"icon":"🌅","time":"Evening","label":"Sunset spa session or drinks"}],"dinner":"Fresh fish or octopus curry. Vegetarian dishes are easy to find.","image":"beach"},{"day":"Day 3","date":"Mon · 22 Feb","place":"Port Louis","emoji":"🧺","title":"Markets, museums, waterfront.","note":"Port Louis is busiest on weekdays, so this is the city day. Start early before the heat and the afternoon showers.","moments":[{"icon":"🧺","time":"Morning","label":"Central Market: spices, herbal teas, street snacks"},{"icon":"🎨","time":"Midday","label":"Blue Penny Museum: art and history"},{"icon":"🏛️","time":"Afternoon","label":"Aapravasi Ghat, the UNESCO heritage site"},{"icon":"🌆","time":"Evening","label":"Dinner at the Caudan Waterfront"}],"dinner":"Waterfront dinner. Try dholl puri and gateaux piments from the market earlier for veg.","image":"market"},{"day":"Day 4","date":"Tue · 23 Feb","place":"South: Chamarel","emoji":"🌈","title":"The view day.","note":"The south-west is the scenic side: coloured earth, a waterfall, and the Le Morne mountain. Book a driver for the day.","moments":[{"icon":"🚗","time":"Morning","label":"Driver to Chamarel (about Rs 4k for the day, an estimate)"},{"icon":"🌈","time":"Midday","label":"Seven Coloured Earths and the Chamarel waterfall"},{"icon":"🥃","time":"Lunch","label":"La Rhumerie de Chamarel, the rum distillery restaurant"},{"icon":"⛰️","time":"Afternoon","label":"Le Morne viewpoint on the way back"}],"dinner":"Back at the stay for a quiet dinner.","image":"chamarel"},{"day":"Day 5","date":"Wed · 24 Feb","place":"Pamplemousses","emoji":"🌿","title":"Garden, art, and the special dinner.","note":"A gentle last full day: the famous giant water-lily garden, a creative session, then dress up once.","moments":[{"icon":"🌿","time":"Morning","label":"Pamplemousses botanical garden and the giant water-lily pond"},{"icon":"🎨","time":"Afternoon","label":"A painting or craft session (ask your stay; availability not checked)"},{"icon":"🕯️","time":"Evening","label":"Private beach dinner"}],"dinner":"Reserved table by the sea. Flag veg needs in advance.","image":"garden"},{"day":"Day 6","date":"Thu · 25 Feb","place":"Mauritius → Kolkata","emoji":"🏠","title":"A slow last morning.","note":"There is no direct flight to Kolkata, so the way home goes via Delhi or Mumbai. Check connection times before booking.","moments":[{"icon":"🥐","time":"Morning","label":"Slow breakfast, last souvenirs (vanilla, tea, rum)"},{"icon":"🚗","time":"Midday","label":"Transfer to the airport (timing depends on the flights)"},{"icon":"✈️","time":"Flight","label":"Mauritius → Delhi or Mumbai → Kolkata, one stop"}],"dinner":"Dinner at home.","image":"lemorne"}]}],"facts":[{"icon":"🌧️","label":"February weather","value":"Hot (about 30°C), humid, with frequent showers. January and February are the rainiest months and fall in cyclone season, so travel insurance matters. March is generally considered better."},{"icon":"🛂","label":"Entry","value":"Indian passport holders are, as far as I know, visa-free. Check the current rules and any online arrival form before booking."},{"icon":"🕐","label":"Time","value":"Mauritius is 1h30 behind India."},{"icon":"🍛","label":"Food","value":"Dholl puri, gateaux piments, Mauritian biryani, curries and fresh seafood. Vegetarian is easy; the cuisine is Indian, Creole and Chinese."}],"links":[{"label":"Best time to visit, month by month","url":"https://www.30sundays.club/blog/best-time-to-visit-mauritius"},{"label":"Delhi to Mauritius fares","url":"https://kayak.co.in/flight-routes/New-Delhi-Indira-Gandhi-Intl-DEL/Mauritius-MU0"},{"label":"Aapravasi Ghat","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aapravasi_Ghat"},{"label":"Blue Penny Museum","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Penny_Museum"},{"label":"Mauritius travel guide","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Mauritius"}],"priceNote":"Prices here are estimates, not live quotes","budgetNote":"Every figure here is an estimate, including flights.","notes":["Flight and stay prices are estimates from search results, not live quotes. Google Flights could not be reached for this destination.","The day outline is adapted from the NextStopAI planner, with Port Louis moved to a weekday. Its own cost estimate (about ₹2L) was far below the fares and was not used.","Restaurant names beyond the Caudan Waterfront and La Rhumerie de Chamarel are not included because they could not be verified."]}$q$::jsonb)
